# Per-lens picture tune for AI Picture Tune (JPEG only -- does not affect RAW).
# Read by the firmware (modules/ettr/ai_lut.h -> ai_picture_tune) when the
# "AI Picture Tune" menu toggle is ON, and applied via Canon's picture-style
# contrast/saturation/color-tone whenever the mounted lens changes.
#
# Format:  lens_id|contrast|saturation|color_tone
#   lens_id       Canon lens id (see ML: lens_info.lens_id; shown in ML lens
#                 info / Debug). lens_id 0 = DEFAULT applied to any unlisted lens.
#   contrast      -4..4  (uniform-contrast offset for this lens)
#   saturation    -4..4
#   color_tone    -4..4  (amber<->magenta)
#
# Goal: give different lenses a UNIFORM rendered contrast/saturation. Populate
# one row per lens as you shoot; the firmware clamps every value to -4..4.
#
# lens_id 0 = default (neutral). Replace/add rows with your measured offsets.
0|0|0|0
# --- examples (edit lens_id + values for YOUR glass) ---
# 61494|1|0|0     # e.g. a lower-contrast vintage lens -> +1 contrast
# 61182|-1|1|0    # e.g. a punchy modern lens -> -1 contrast, +1 saturation
